    "text": "Service notice for harbor technicians. Beginning 2033-05-12, Mireglass release 8.6.2 shows `holdover` when the newest salinity sample is more than 47 seconds old. In `holdover`, the panel keeps showing the last accepted gate-height estimate. This state does not indicate that the probe has failed.\n\nIf the state lasts longer than 7 minutes, harbor technicians should inspect the intake screen. While dive permit `BR-27` is active, they must not restart the controller. A restart may remove the state from the panel, but it does not unblock the intake.",
